  "schema": "arcpuzzles-parametric-prototype-evidence-v1",
  "scope": "# Review \u2014 b3d7f3a15b3d proposed parametric prototype\nTask/source: `review-b248ec296d74f803`; production generator SHA-256 `e1d8f2ffd5cf0a2329ca1c3cede73a2333a5cc6afbdc906bc143015a210b4ce5` is unchanged.\nReference rule: canonical `RULE_HASH=032c15e97118`; exact canonical Racket SHA-256 `f52d92a5c27d82f897b1b614769022a43cb056be04e7ecede45e5f2b69921dfb` is unchanged.\nDefect \u2192 repair: setting-order `episode-NN` public names were replaced by exact-visible-byte SHA-256 IDs and `public/<ID>.json` paths.\nPrivacy/determinism: private seeds, parameters, programs and query answers cannot affect a public ID; batches are sorted by ID and duplicate visible payloads are rejected.\nWrite safety: all public/private/rule bytes are prevalidated before the output tree is created, so a malformed later private record cannot leave a partial batch.\nChecks: focused suite passed `10` tests plus `21` subtests; the six-setting Racket-backed run preserved `8/8` canonical pairs and emitted `3` demos plus `4` distinct queries per episode.\nEvidence: `checks/parametric-final-tests/pytest.log`, `checks/parametric-public-id-final/report.json`, and `checks/parametric-public-id-final/verify.log`.\nRemaining limits: this is a bounded task-local six-setting prototype, not a production parametric API, unrestricted uniqueness proof, variant approval, or training admission.\nDisposition: routine selected-task correction; separate peer target `010ef9d0160b` needs attention for an invalid-override API finding recorded in `AUDIT.md`.\n\n## Implemented change",
  "task_id": "b3d7f3a15b3d",
  "variant_approved": false,
  "verification_status": "reviewer_reported"
